{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>A land of wheat and barley.</b> Since the land corresponds to the tenth part, therefore it was praised in ten things: for the grain — five species, and of them he took the two that are the principal ones, and left oat and rye and spelt, which are included under wheat and barley — that makes five; and vine and fig and pomegranate, olive and honey — that makes ten. And so it was praised as 'a land flowing with milk and honey,' that is, the Will that bestows mercy and judgment, in the manner of (Genesis 36:39) ״בת מי זהב״ — 'whose daughter was Me-Zahav'; and the discerning will understand."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:50.923981656Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}